    "result_text": "Done. The change is implemented and the full test suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`), including the new `coreIdempotentRepeat` acceptance test that previously failed with 409.\n\n## What I did\n\n`POST /api/owners` now honors an optional `Idempotency-Key` header: a repeat with an already-seen key replays the originally created owner with **200** instead of creating a duplicate (which otherwise 409s on the identity check).\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (no `@RestController`, no `@ControllerAdvice`), I added:\n\n**Pipeline steps** (`owners.POST.yml`):\n- `checkIdempotency` \u2014 new **first** step. Reads the header via OfficeFloor's native `@HttpHeaderParameter(\"Idempotency-Key\")` (which binds `null` when absent, so ordinary creates are unaffected). If the key was already used, it throws a checked `IdempotentReplayException(ownerId)`, cleanly short-circuiting the create pipeline.\n- `recordIdempotency` \u2014 inserted **after** `save` (so the generated id exists), records `key \u2192 owner id`.\n\n**Supporting classes:**\n- `IdempotencyStore` \u2014 a Spring `@Component` holding a concurrent `key \u2192 ownerId` map (`putIfAbsent` keeps the first winner), injected by type like the other beans.\n- `IdempotentReplayException` + `IdempotentReplayExceptionHandler` (wired via `officefloor/escalation/\u2026IdempotentReplayException.yml`) \u2014 the handler loads the original owner and sends the same `OwnerDto` body with a 200.\n\n## How I verified it\n\n- Established a baseline first: the new test failed with `expected:<200> but was:<409>`, confirming the gap.\n- Confirmed a missing header binds to `null` (read the OfficeFloor `HttpArgumentManagedObjectSource` source) \u2014 so the ~unrelated create tests keep working.\n- Ran the full suite offline after the change: **1 test, 0 failures, 0 errors** (surefire report).\n\nOne design note: the idempotency store is in-memory (process-scoped), which is sufficient here and keeps the change contained \u2014 no schema migration across the four DB profiles. If you'd want cross-instance/persistent idempotency, that would need a backing table instead.",
