    "probe_text": "I now have the complete picture. Here is the ordered account of everything that happens on `POST /api/owners`.\n\n## Endpoint gate (before any step)\n\n- **Authorization** \u2014 the whole file is guarded by `authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`. Without that role the request never enters the pipeline (403).\n\n## The pipeline, in execution order\n\nSteps 1\u20139 run with no transaction; from step 10 (`requireUniqueIdentity`) onward every step is under `govern: [ transaction ]`, so all the reads-for-conflict and all the writes commit together at the end.\n\n**1. `CheckIdempotencyKey` \u2014 validation / short-circuit**\nReads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header. Absent/blank \u2192 proceeds. If the key was already used, throws `IdempotentReplayException` \u2192 200 replay of the original owner (no new owner created).\n\n**2. `RequireOwnerFields` \u2014 validation**\nBinds the request body **once** (no `@Valid`). Requires non-blank `firstName`, `lastName`, `city`, `telephone`, and an address in *either* structured (`addressLine1`) or flat (`address`) form \u2014 address is judged blank *after* normalization. Any missing/blank \u2192 400 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` listing every offending field. Republishes the body as a variable for later steps.\n\n**3. `RequireCurrentRegistrationDate` \u2014 validation**\nOnly if `registrationDate` is supplied: rejects a date later than today \u2192 400 `FutureRegistrationDateException`. Absent date is left alone.\n\n**4. `NormalizeOwnerTelephone` \u2014 validation + mutation**\nNormalizes telephone to E.164 (strip separators; keep/assume `+61`, drop leading `0`; length rules per country code). Writes the E.164 value back onto the request DTO. Unparseable \u2192 400 `InvalidTelephoneException`.\n\n**5. `NormalizeOwnerEmail` \u2014 validation + mutation**\nEmail is optional: null/blank \u2192 set to `null`. If present, must match the syntactic regex; stores the trimmed, lower-cased value back on the DTO. Invalid \u2192 400 `InvalidEmailException`.\n\n**6. `RequireEmailDomain` \u2014 validation**\nIf an email is present, rejects a domain on the disposable blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 400 `DisposableEmailDomainException`.\n\n**7. `NormalizeOwnerAddress` \u2014 mutation**\nCanonicalizes the address (trim/collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand abbreviations). Structured form preferred: normalizes `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` and composes the flat `address` from them; otherwise normalizes the flat `address` in place. Writes back onto the DTO. (No rejection here \u2014 presence was already enforced in step 2.)\n\n**8. `RequirePostcode` \u2014 validation**\nOnly if `postcode` supplied: must be 4 digits; for a city with a known region (Sydney\u2192NSW 2000\u20132099, Melbourne\u2192VIC 3000\u20133099, Brisbane\u2192QLD 4000\u20134099) it must fall in range. Unknown-region cities accept any 4-digit code. Invalid \u2192 400 `InvalidPostcodeException`.\n\n**9. `RequireUniqueIdentity` \u2014 validation (transactional read)**\nComputes deterministic `householdId` (last name + postcode) and `identityKey` (telephone|email|householdId). Scanning all non-soft-deleted owners: exact `identityKey` match \u2192 409 `DuplicateIdentityException`; same `householdId` \u2192 409 **unless** the request set `sharesHousehold: true`.\n\n**10. `RequireCityCapacity` \u2014 validation**\nRejects if the owner's city already holds \u2265 50 owners \u2192 409 `CityAtCapacityException`.\n\n**11. `RequireDailyCapacity` \u2014 validation**\nComputes the *effective* registration date (supplied-or-today, rolled to next business day). Rejects if \u2265 100 existing owners already carry that date \u2192 429 `DailyLimitExceededException`.\n\n**12. `BuildOwner` \u2014 side-effect (construct)**\nMaps the validated DTO into a new `Owner` entity via `OwnerMapper` (published for the rest of the pipeline). This is the point past which no more 4xx checks occur \u2014 everything after enriches and persists.\n\n**13. `AssignHouseholdId` \u2014 mutation**\nStamps the deterministic `householdId` (last name + postcode; null when no postcode) on the owner.\n\n**14. `CountHouseholdMembers` \u2014 mutation**\nSets `householdSize` = existing owners sharing the `householdId` + 1 (this owner). Null household leaves it null.\n\n**15. `ApplyRegistrationDate` \u2014 mutation**\nSets `registrationDate` to the effective date (supplied-or-today, rolled forward off weekends).\n\n**16. `AssignCustomerCode` \u2014 mutation**\nSets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode-then-city; HASH8 = first 8 hex of SHA-256 over telephone+lastName), appending `-<n>` (n\u22652) on collision with an existing code.\n\n**17. `CountNamesakes` \u2014 mutation**\nSets `namesakeCount` = existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n\n**18. `FlagBulkSignup` \u2014 mutation**\nSets `bulkSignupWarning` true when > 80 existing owners already carry this registration date.\n\n**19. `FlagPossibleDuplicate` \u2014 mutation**\nDefaults `possibleDuplicate=false`/`possibleDuplicateOf=null`. Unless `sharesHousehold` or no postcode: if a non-deleted owner shares last name + postcode but has a different telephone, sets `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf` = the earliest-id match.\n\n**20. `SaveOwner` \u2014 side-effect (persist)**\n`ownerRepository.save(owner)` \u2014 the owner is written and gets its generated id.\n\n**21. `RecordIdempotencyKey` \u2014 side-effect**\nIf an `Idempotency-Key` header was present, records `key \u2192 owner.id` so a later repeat replays instead of duplicating. No-op without a key.\n\n**22. `LogOwnerAudit` \u2014 side-effect**\nEmits an `AUDIT` log line: id, customerCode, registrationDate, derived membershipNumber, membership points and level.\n\n**23. `RespondWithOwnerCreated` \u2014 response**\nMaps the owner to `OwnerDto` and sends **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n## Summary\n\n- **Validations, in order:** auth role \u2192 idempotency replay \u2192 required fields \u2192 non-future registration date \u2192 telephone E.164 \u2192 email syntax \u2192 email domain blocklist \u2192 postcode format/region \u2192 identity/household uniqueness (409) \u2192 city capacity (409) \u2192 daily capacity (429).\n- **Side-effects, in order:** DTO normalization (telephone, email, address) \u2192 build entity \u2192 stamp householdId, householdSize, registrationDate, customerCode, namesakeCount, bulkSignupWarning, possibleDuplicate/-Of \u2192 **persist** \u2192 record idempotency key \u2192 write audit log \u2192 201 response.\n\nOne thing worth flagging: several checks (`RequireUniqueIdentity`, `RequireCityCapacity`, `RequireDailyCapacity`) each do a full `findAll()` scan and depend on committed state, but they run inside the same transaction as the insert \u2014 under concurrency two simultaneous creates can both pass these checks before either commits, so the uniqueness/capacity limits are not race-safe. I've only described the code as written; let me know if you'd like me to look closer at that."
